title: "Hybrid Quantum-Classical Knowledge Graph Model with Mixture of Recursions (MoR) for Genomic Sequence Analysis"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-04-04
url: "https://github.com/senthilv83/Hybrid-Quantum-Cirq-Genomics-KG-Model"
keywords:
  - Quantum Machine Learning (QML)
  - Google Cirq
  - PyTorch
  - Mixture of Recursions (MoR)
  - Quantum Neural Network (QNN)
  - Knowledge Graph
  - Topological Embeddings
  - Spectral Laplacian
  - Readout Error Mitigation (QEC)
  - Genomics
  - Bioinformatics
  - NISQ
abstract: "A state-of-the-art Hybrid Quantum-Classical Genomics Knowledge Graph Model integrating Google Cirq and PyTorch. This framework introduces the Dynamic Mixture of Recursions (MoR) paradigm to Quantum Neural Networks, enabling confidence-based early exits to save quantum compute overhead. It transforms genomic sequence data into topological Knowledge Graphs (KG) via Laplacian Spectral Embeddings and processes them through an end-to-end differentiable, strongly entangling variational quantum circuit with Readout Error Mitigation (QEC). The architecture discovers hidden biological relationships and long-range dependencies with >86% accuracy."
